{"ts": "2026-11-23T00:22:25.849977Z", "run_id": "r-20261122T2330Z-2571", "unit": "openspec:add-http-openapi-tools", "seq": 78, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-002", "id": "Q-002", "status": "answered", "reason": "Verified in the repository: docs/api/openapi.json has 50 path keys (grep of the paths object) and no tool-registrations/openapi or tool-servers/{id}/openapi entry; src/main.ts does not yet call registerOpenApiToolRoutes; openapi-tool-routes.ts defines exactly three urls; the spec and test-plan-runs require those three paths in the served and committed document; task 5.1 says C-d150bfa4 stays green. 50 + 3 = 53, so option 1 is the only correct exact count and option 2 would weaken a test (AGENTS.md \"Never weaken ... an existing test\").", "called": true, "tasks": ["5.1"], "target": null, "kind": "technical", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.05525475, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "e4daf1fb588e82b5cba5610454706fb5926d5be2cf1d1af604b972849bc8363c", "checked": [{"ref": "src/main.conventions.test.ts:126", "quote": "assert.equal(paths.length, 50, `the document lists 50 paths: ${JSON.stringify(paths)}`);", "claim": "The frozen conventions test hard-codes an exact path count of 50."}, {"ref": "src/api/people-openapi.test.ts:55", "quote": "assert.equal(Object.keys(paths).length, 50, \"the document lists 50 paths\");", "claim": "The frozen people test also hard-codes an exact path count of 50."}, {"ref": "docs/api/openapi.json:8709", "quote": "\"/api/v1/tool-servers\": {", "claim": "The committed document lists the existing tool-server paths but no tool-registrations/openapi or tool-servers/{id}/openapi path; the paths object holds 50 keys."}, {"ref": "src/api/openapi-tool-routes.ts:177", "quote": "url: \"/api/v1/tool-registrations/openapi/preview\",", "claim": "The route module defines the first of exactly three new distinct urls (lines 177, 193 and 240)."}, {"ref": "src/api/openapi-tool-routes.ts:240", "quote": "url: \"/api/v1/tool-servers/:id/openapi\",", "claim": "The third new route is a distinct path, so the document grows by three paths."}, {"ref": "src/main.ts:294", "quote": "registerToolServerRoutes(server, { pool: pep.pool, clock: pep.clock, engineKey: config.engineKey });", "claim": "main.ts registers the tool-server routes but not yet the OpenAPI tool routes, so the new paths are not in the document until task 5.1."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/tool-http/spec.md#requirement-the-engine-wires-the-adapter-and-the-routes-and-the-api-document-lists-them", "quote": "`docs/api/openapi.json` SHALL hold the three operations.", "claim": "The spec requires the three operations in the committed document, which adds three paths."}, {"ref": "openspec/changes/add-http-openapi-tools/tasks.md:23", "quote": "`src/main.conventions.test.ts::C-d150bfa4` stays green", "claim": "Task 5.1 requires the frozen conventions test to pass after the document is regenerated, which needs the count updated to 53."}, {"ref": "AGENTS.md:17", "quote": "Weaken, skip or delete an existing test.", "claim": "A relative lower bound (option 2) would weaken the existing exact-count assertion, so the exact 53 (option 1) is the right change."}]}
